							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">it&#039;s really hard to picture a bean pie.<br /><br />what is the wire? is it that video that carmelo anthony was in?<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I&#039;m not even gonna get into comparing the NOI to the Nazis and the meaning of racism but let me just say that I don&#039;t find it ridiculous at all to rely on the organization&#039;s self-perception. If I want to learn about the government of the USA I will read about the constitution and the bill of rights before I even come close to learning about individuals working for the ideas of the original framers.<br /><br />Just like when a martial artist starts his physical application of his artform, he ain&#039;t gonna learn Poison Hand of Death first. He&#039;s gonna start with some basic stance work, blocks and strikes.<br /><br />You asked about the NOI, not the individuals who run the organization. The NOI&#039;s website pretty much details what they are about. Whether the individuals within it practice what they preach is an entirely different subject. However if you are the type of person who compares the NOI to Hitler&#039;s Nazi party of 1930&#039;s Germany then I don&#039;t even see the point in continuing this dialogue because it will head nowhere productive.</div><br />stop misinterpreting things on purpose so you can attack what you claim to think they said instead of what was actually meant. you sound like right wing when they ripped john kerry for criticizing the white house&#039;s handling of the war in iraq, saying that he was placing blame on the troops. i provided an example of a group whose rhetoric didn&#039;t match their actions. that&#039;s all i did.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Whether the individuals within it practice what they preach is an entirely different subject.</div><br />no it&#039;s not. there are a million cliches that attack that statement. i didn&#039;t ask what they said they did. i asked what they did.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">However if you are the type of person who compares the NOI to Hitler&#039;s Nazi party of 1930&#039;s Germany then I don&#039;t even see the point in continuing this dialogue because it will head nowhere productive.</div><br />if you&#039;re saying that people who make good analogies are incapable of understanding the noi, i think it&#039;s you who are insulting them.<br /><br />a martial artist should also recognize that sometimes his instructor is wrong. he&#039;s gotta know that the techniques he learns won&#039;t send him on the wrong path so that he gets his ass beat around the dojo. you didn&#039;t say that i should use the noi site as a foundation. you said i should read it INSTEAD of asking for more objective opinions.<br /><br />please give me the meaning of racism. because the definition for application among humans that i&#039;ve always been taught is &quot;discrimination based upon ethnicity&quot; and the aforementioned behavior definitely fits into that category. who knows though, the guy could&#039;ve had a different reason for rejecting sage or whichever poster it was that gave that account. while he&#039;s mostly white, the man is multi-ethnic indeed.</div>
						</td>
